      "title": "Heat loss",
      "description": "Bare pipe (left) loses heat strongly by convection and radiation; under the insulation (right) the heat flow is a fraction of that. Heat loss per metre ≈ 2πk(T_pipe − T_surface)/ln(r_out/r_in). Insulation also keeps the surface below touch-safe temperature (personnel protection, typically ≤ 60 °C — verify local regulations).",
