  "summary": "A pipe insulation system reduces heat loss (or gain) from piping, keeps process temperatures stable, protects personnel from hot surfaces and prevents condensation on cold lines. A typical hot-service system has an anti-corrosion coating on the pipe, one or more insulation layers with staggered joints, and a weatherproof metal cladding held by bands, plus insulated supports.",
